  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on comparing the minimum probability of outcomes in each lottery, favoring the one with the higher minimum probability. In this case, Lottery B has a minimum probability of 100%, clearly higher than A’s 1%, so the reason aligns with choosing B. The individual’s reasoning centers on preferring a sure outcome ('SICHER geld') over uncertainty, which reflects sensitivity to the certainty of receiving a payoff—closely related to the concept of minimum probability. Although the individual does not explicitly mention 'minimum probability' or perform a technical comparison of probabilities, the emphasis on certainty maps directly to the core logic of the decision reason: favoring the option with no risk of getting nothing. The justification aligns with the rule of the decision reason, even if expressed in lay terms. Therefore, it is highly likely the individual used reasoning consistent with the specified decision rule.",
  "final_assessment_score": 95
